  "brief_description": "This painting is a companion piece to Fishermen hauling a Net, which is exactly the same size and depicts a scene with three similarly positioned boats, a low horizon and high billowing clouds. However, the muddy island in the middle of this scene is more substantial and, as the title suggests, someone has built a hut on it.\n\nThere are many subtle differences between the two pictures. In this one it appears to be high water; in the other it is clearly low tide. And while both feature a windmill and a church in similar positions on the horizon, the church depicted in this painting has a tower rather than a spire. The boats are also being used for a different purpose here -- not for fishing, but for transport. The rowing boat in the foreground is carrying passengers, while the larger sailing boat is a type used for transporting goods and people on inland waterways.",
